elaine: heads up — hitting weird schema/typing drop when streaming tool calls + auth refresh. root error: function output gets truncated to {} after retry. anyone seen this?
ryan: hmm can you paste minimal repro?
elaine: sure — ts client, streaming funcall, token auto-refresh enabled. gist:
```ts
const stream = client.tool.callStream({
  name: 'parse_invoice',
  input: {text: invoiceText},
});
for await (const chunk of stream) {
  if (chunk.type === 'tool_response') {
    // expecting {items: Array<{line:number,amt:number}>}
    console.log(chunk.payload);
  }
}
```
When the access token expires mid-stream, the SDK retries auth and resumes, but the reconstructed payload becomes "payload: {}" and typing guards fail.
jia: is the retry re-sending the whole request with new auth or resuming the socket? If the stream is resumed, we might be mixing frames.
sam: saw similar — root cause was that the streaming parser resets buffer on reconnect. quick patch: keep incremental buffer across reconnects and replay only missing frames.
ryan: can you share a stack trace/log showing frames? also which SDK version?
elaine: v0.12.3 — logs: "auth: token expired, refreshing and retrying; stream: reset parser state" then later "received tool_response: {}"
sam: workaround: set client.options.retryOnAuth = false for long-lived streams, then refresh token proactively before call. ugly but good short term.
jia: long-term I'd prefer SDK change: when auth retry happens, mark reconnect but do NOT reset JSON state machine; instead, keep last partial token and continue. also add typed guard helper: client.helpers.assertToolResponse(schema, data) to coerce/raise.
elaine: agree. filing a tiny RFC + PR. I'll ping maintainers. thanks :pray: 
dev-bot: created issue #1256: keep-stream-parser-state-on-auth-retry — assigned to eng-ml
ryan: ack, I'll review the PR when ready.
